# Scholar:: new code

## Layout

- Namespace: **`Scholar::`** (e.g. `Scholar::Record`, `Scholar::Export::Manifest`)
- Paths: `lib/scholar/`, `app/models/scholar/`, `spec/lib/scholar/` or `spec/scholar/`
- Do not add modernization logic to Hyrax overrides unless bridging legacy in Phase 1

## Style (match legacy app, stay boring)

- Ruby 2.7 / Rails 5.2 compatible until a planned Rails upgrade hop
- Prefer plain objects and small service classes over new gems
- Explicit over clever; minimal metaprogramming
- No comments for obvious code; comment export/import invariants and DOI rules only

## Dependencies

- Avoid new gems unless STATUS/plan approves
- Reuse existing stack: ActiveRecord, ActiveJob/Sidekiq (for now), Devise users

## Tests

- Add focused specs for export/import and `Scholar::DoiService` behavior
- Do not duplicate full Hyrax feature specs for new paths
- New specs should run under **`bin/rspec-fast`** (no Fedora/Solr); see `docs/modernization/TESTING.md`

## Diffs

- Smallest correct change for the current phase slice
- Do not refactor unrelated legacy code or reformat Hyrax files
- Naming: follow [scholar-naming-conventions.mdc](../scholar-naming-conventions.mdc); run [scholar-code-quality.mdc](../scholar-code-quality.mdc) before done
